## Distribution / packaging
# These are anchored on purpose. An unanchored `lib/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, which silently excluded frontend/src/lib and broke
# the build for anyone cloning the repo. Python only ever writes these under
# the repo root or backend/, so say exactly that.
.Python
/build/
/dist/
/sdist/
/wheels/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/develop-eggs/
/parts/
/var/
backend/build/
backend/dist/
backend/sdist/
backend/wheels/
backend/downloads/
backend/eggs/
backend/.eggs/
backend/develop-eggs/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

